BUG-38: engine progress POSITION during the OOXML import and Writer layout.

A DOCX with thousands of anchored shapes (our own PDF -> DOCX output) imports and lays
out for minutes with no progress report: the OOXML import reports progress only when
docProps declares a ParagraphCount (pdf-docx output declares 0), and the initial layout
during view creation never starts a progress bar. The web driver's 30 s no-progress
watchdog then stops a conversion that is working.

These hooks give the bridge (engine/bridge/wasm_bridge.cpp, which holds the strong
definitions and all the logic) first-time engine work to count:
  - OOXMLDocumentImpl::incrementProgress (every paragraph end) and
    OOXMLFastContextHandlerShape::sendShape (every shape): import position;
  - SwLayAction::InternalAction (each page the layout loop visits): highest page reached;
  - SwObjectFormatter::FormatObj_ (every anchored object, fly or drawing): the object's
    SwFrameFormat, so the bridge counts distinct objects formatted at least once. Keyed by
    the document-model format, not the layout frame, because a looping layout can delete
    and recreate frames while the formats persist;
  - SwFrame::AppendFly / SwFrame::AppendDrawObj (frame creation, before the layout loop: a
    paragraph with thousands of anchors spends its first seconds here): distinct objects
    attached for the first time, counted separately from those formatted;
The hooks are weak no-ops here, so any other link of sw stays whole. WASM only.

